The key tension
Here's what I want to make sure we're seeing clearly:

Daily back to 2020 → Yahoo Finance likely already works. The code currently hardcodes period="1y". Changing to start="2020-01-01" with yfinance should just work for most tokens.

Hourly back to 2020 → That's ~52,000 candles per symbol. Almost no provider reliably has crypto hourly data from 6 years ago. EODHD's intraday plan is typically limited to 1-2 years of hourly lookback.

A question worth sitting with
What does the short strategy actually need from hourly data?

Right now it works on daily closes — entry and exit are next-day opens (approximately). If you move to hourly, you could:

Get more precise entry/exit timing within the day
Potentially more trades (shorter SMA period, more crossings)
But compute and cache costs grow 24×
Is the goal to backtest more accurately, or to get more historical trades for statistical confidence?

For statistical confidence, extending daily data back to 2020 gets you ~4× more trades at no extra complexity. Going hourly adds precision but also noise.


